# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) and this package divide the work rather than overlap, along a single line:\n"
msgstr "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) e questo pacchetto si dividono il lavoro anziché sovrapporsi, lungo un'unica linea:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| ffsim owns                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | `qiskit-fermions` owns                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| The high-level ansatz *operators* ([`UCJOpSpinBalanced`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced \"(in ffsim)\"), [`UCCSDOpRestrictedReal`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal.html#ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal \"(in ffsim)\") and their siblings), built from coupled-cluster amplitudes or a parameter vector | The fermionic *circuit* ([`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")) those operators become, and its transpilation into a qubit circuit under any fermion-to-qubit encoding |\n"
"| Fast simulation in a compact fixed-particle-number space                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | The mapper framework and the operator data structures the circuit is built from                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n"
msgstr ""
"| ffsim si occupa di                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | `qiskit-fermions` si occupa di                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Gli *operatori* di ansatz di alto livello ([`UCJOpSpinBalanced`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced \"(in ffsim)\"), [`UCCSDOpRestrictedReal`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal.html#ffsim.UCCSDOpRestrictedReal \"(in ffsim)\") e i loro simili), costruiti da ampiezze coupled-cluster o da un vettore di parametri | Il *circuito* fermionico ([`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")) in cui quegli operatori si trasformano, e la sua transpilazione in un circuito di qubit con qualsiasi codifica da fermioni a qubit |\n"
"| Simulazione veloce in uno spazio compatto a numero di particelle fisso                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Il framework dei mapper e le strutture dati degli operatori da cui è costruito il circuito                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The practical consequence runs both ways. The ansatz math lives in ffsim, so [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") and [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") take an ffsim operator directly as their input. Conversely, ffsim’s own Qiskit gates are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation, so lowering one of its ansatz operators through a *different* encoding is what bringing it here buys you.\n"
msgstr "La conseguenza pratica vale in entrambe le direzioni. La matematica dell'ansatz risiede in ffsim, quindi [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") e [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") accettano direttamente un operatore ffsim come input. Viceversa, i gate Qiskit propri di ffsim sono specifici della trasformazione di Jordan-Wigner, quindi ciò che ottieni portandolo qui è poter abbassare uno dei suoi operatori di ansatz attraverso una codifica *diversa*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulation is where the two meet, and this guide explains how. ffsim is this package’s simulation backend, reached through its own protocols rather than a wrapper: the [SKQD guide](skqd#skqd-getting-started) calls [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\"), [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\"), and [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") directly on [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")objects and [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\")objects, with no conversion step.\n"
msgstr "La simulazione è il punto in cui i due si incontrano, e questa guida spiega come. ffsim è il backend di simulazione di questo pacchetto, raggiunto tramite i suoi protocolli anziché un wrapper: la [guida SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) chiama [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\"), [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") e [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") direttamente su oggetti [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")e su oggetti [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\")senza alcun passaggio di conversione.\n"

